  "verdict": "Monolithic bus at the canon rod O1.0 (01_01 1.4), SHIPPED fabrication = welded (welded cold-drawn wire, ratified 2026-09-10): buckling non-issue (SF 10x); the bore liner doubles as lateral support -> fatigue SF 8.5-23.3x (infinite life, all alloys). BARE, the drawn wire reaches infinite life for 4 of 6 alloys (SF 1.4-3.9x): dropping the as-printed derate lifted CP-Ti-Gr4, Ta OUT of predicted failure but NOT over the SF-2 line. On the superseded PRINTED branch not one of the six cleared it. BUT the fatigue ground for the liner is RETIRED, not narrowed (verdict 2026-09-11): the free-cantilever SF describes NO shipped branch, because every branch that leaves play takes it up and bears on the bore wall. What the liner carries is WEAR - the contact is geometrically forced, and wear-through is a ~0.5 V anode-cathode short. Liner = insulation + wear surface + lateral support; NOT a fatigue fix (HW.34 sub-2). Per-alloy margin tracks yield = same ranking as thermal -> leading HW.24 candidates win on both.",
